---
import BaseLayout from '../../components/layout/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Narrative Audit for B2B research"
  description="A fixed-scope review that turns underused B2B research, customer insight and expertise into a clear narrative opportunity, evidence map and practical next step."
  pageType="service"
>
  <article class="container-site py-20">
    <div class="audit-inner">

      <header class="mb-16">
        <p class="t-label mb-6">Narrative Audit</p>
        <h1 class="t-display mb-6">Find the argument already inside your evidence.</h1>
        <div class="prose-section mb-8">
          <p>Your organisation may already have the research, customer insight and subject expertise it needs. What is often missing is a clear view of what that evidence adds up to — and which argument is worth developing.</p>
          <p>The Narrative Audit is a focused review that identifies the strongest through-lines in your existing material and turns them into a practical editorial opportunity.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="engagement-strip mb-8">
          <div>
            <span class="strip-label">Format</span>
            <span class="strip-value">Fixed scope and fee</span>
          </div>
          <div>
            <span class="strip-label">Timeline</span>
            <span class="strip-value">Two to three weeks</span>
          </div>
          <div>
            <span class="strip-label">Best for</span>
            <span class="strip-value">Underused B2B evidence</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="hero-ctas">
          <a href="mailto:asavin@editorialintelligence.co?subject=Narrative%20Audit%20enquiry" class="audit-btn">Discuss a Narrative Audit</a>
          <a href="#deliverables" class="audit-link">See what you receive ↓</a>
        </div>
      </header>

      <hr class="divider mb-16" />

      <section class="mb-16">
        <h2 class="audit-h2 mb-6">When useful evidence has no organising argument</h2>
        <div class="prose-section mb-8">
          <p>Research is frequently treated as a campaign asset: launch the report, publish a few articles and move on. Customer insight lives elsewhere. Executive expertise appears in interviews and events. Performance data rarely reconnects with the original thinking.</p>
          <p>The result is not necessarily a shortage of content. It is a synthesis gap. Valuable evidence exists, but the organisation cannot see the distinctive position, recurring narrative or editorial system inside it.</p>
        </div>
        <ul class="audit-list">
          <li>You have commissioned research but are unsure how to extend its value.</li>
          <li>Your content covers many topics without building a recognisable position.</li>
          <li>Customer stories, expert insight and market evidence remain disconnected.</li>
          <li>You suspect there is a stronger argument in the material but cannot yet name it.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <hr class="divider mb-16" />

      <section id="deliverables" class="mb-16">
        <h2 class="audit-h2 mb-4">What you leave with</h2>
        <p class="prose-intro mb-8">Three connected outputs that show what the evidence means and what to do with it.</p>

        <div class="deliverables-list">
          <div class="deliverable-item">
            <span class="item-num">01</span>
            <div>
              <h3 class="item-heading">Narrative Audit</h3>
              <p class="item-body">A concise assessment of the strongest through-lines, contradictions, overlooked signals and existing assets worth reactivating.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="deliverable-item">
            <span class="item-num">02</span>
            <div>
              <h3 class="item-heading">Evidence map</h3>
              <p class="item-body">A structured view of the research, customer proof, expertise and market evidence supporting each potential argument — including the important gaps.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="deliverable-item">
            <span class="item-num">03</span>
            <div>
              <h3 class="item-heading">Opportunity brief</h3>
              <p class="item-body">A prioritised recommendation covering the narrative territory to develop, the audience it matters to and the most useful next move.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <hr class="divider mb-16" />

      <section class="mb-16">
        <h2 class="audit-h2 mb-4">What I review</h2>
        <p class="prose-intro mb-8">The scope is agreed in advance. A typical audit draws from a focused selection of material such as:</p>
        <div class="review-grid">
          <div class="review-item">Original research and reports</div>
          <div class="review-item">Customer interviews and case studies</div>
          <div class="review-item">Existing articles and campaign assets</div>
          <div class="review-item">Executive and subject-matter expertise</div>
          <div class="review-item">Event, webinar and audience signals</div>
          <div class="review-item">Relevant performance and market evidence</div>
        </div>
        <p class="scope-note">You do not need a perfect archive. Part of the initial conversation is deciding which material is most likely to reveal something useful.</p>
      </section>

      <hr class="divider mb-16" />

      <section class="mb-16">
        <h2 class="audit-h2 mb-8">How the audit works</h2>
        <div class="process-list">
          <div class="process-step">
            <span class="item-num">1</span>
            <div>
              <h3 class="item-heading">Define the question</h3>
              <p class="item-body">Agree the business context, audience, available evidence and the decision the audit needs to inform.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="process-step">
            <span class="item-num">2</span>
            <div>
              <h3 class="item-heading">Map the evidence</h3>
              <p class="item-body">Review the selected material and organise the strongest findings, claims, examples, tensions and gaps.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="process-step">
            <span class="item-num">3</span>
            <div>
              <h3 class="item-heading">Find the argument</h3>
              <p class="item-body">Identify the most distinctive and defensible narrative territory already present across the evidence.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="process-step">
            <span class="item-num">4</span>
            <div>
              <h3 class="item-heading">Set the next move</h3>
              <p class="item-body">Present the audit, evidence map and opportunity brief in a working session focused on priorities and decisions.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <hr class="divider mb-16" />

      <section class="mb-16">
        <h2 class="audit-h2 mb-6">What happens afterwards</h2>
        <div class="prose-section mb-8">
          <p>The audit is a complete engagement in itself. You can use its findings with your internal team, agency or existing partners.</p>
          <p>If a larger opportunity emerges, the next phase can be scoped separately: developing the narrative, creating a research activation plan, designing the editorial architecture or building the evidence workflow needed to sustain it. There is no requirement to continue.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="next-grid">
          <a href="/narratives/hidden-hours" class="next-card">
            <span class="next-label">See the approach in practice</span>
            <strong>Hidden Hours</strong>
            <span>One research programme developed into an ongoing narrative platform and reusable evidence base →</span>
          </a>
          <a href="/editorial-intelligence-os" class="next-card">
            <span class="next-label">Explore the wider system</span>
            <strong>Editorial Intelligence OS</strong>
            <span>How evidence, narratives, activation and learning work together →</span>
          </a>
        </div>
      </section>

      <hr class="divider mb-16" />

      <section class="mb-16">
        <h2 class="audit-h2 mb-6">A focused, senior engagement</h2>
        <div class="engagement-panel">
          <div class="prose-section">
            <p>I carry out the analysis and synthesis myself. The scope, inputs, deliverables, timeline and fixed fee are agreed before the work begins.</p>
            <p>A typical audit takes two to three weeks. It includes an initial working session, the independent review and synthesis, the three written outputs and a findings session.</p>
          </div>
          <a href="mailto:asavin@editorialintelligence.co?subject=Narrative%20Audit%20enquiry" class="audit-btn mt-6">Discuss a Narrative Audit</a>
        </div>
      </section>

      <hr class="divider mb-16" />

      <section class="mb-8">
        <p class="t-label mb-6">Start with what you already have</p>
        <h2 class="audit-h2 mb-4">There may be a stronger argument inside it.</h2>
        <div class="prose-section mb-8">
          <p>Tell me what research, insight or expertise you are sitting on. I will help you decide whether a Narrative Audit is the right first step.</p>
        </div>
        <a href="mailto:asavin@editorialintelligence.co?subject=Narrative%20Audit%20enquiry" class="audit-btn">Discuss what you already have</a>
      </section>

    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .audit-inner { max-width: 42rem; }

  .prose-section { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1.25rem; }
  .prose-section p { font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--color-ink-secondary); }
  .prose-intro { font-size: 0.9375rem; line-height: 1.75; color: var(--color-ink-secondary); }
  .scope-note { margin-top: 1.25rem; font-size: 0.875rem; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--color-ink-tertiary); font-style: italic; }

  .audit-h2 { font-family: var(--font-serif); font-size: clamp(1.15rem, 2.5vw, 1.4rem); font-weight: 400; color: var(--color-ink); letter-spacing: -0.01em; }

  .hero-ctas { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 1.5rem; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .audit-btn { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; background: var(--color-accent); color: var(--color-surface); font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.75rem; letter-spacing: 0.06em; font-weight: 600; padding: 0.75rem 1.25rem; border-radius: 3px; text-decoration: none; transition: opacity 0.15s; }
  .audit-btn:hover { opacity: 0.85; }
  .audit-link { font-size: 0.875rem; color: var(--color-ink-tertiary); text-decoration: none; transition: color 0.15s; }
  .audit-link:hover { color: var(--color-accent); }
  .mt-6 { margin-top: 1.5rem; }

  .engagement-strip { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 1px; background: var(--color-rule); border: 1px solid var(--color-rule); border-radius: 4px; overflow: hidden; }
  .engagement-strip > div { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.35rem; padding: 1rem; background: var(--color-surface-secondary); }
  .strip-label, .next-label { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.75rem; line-height: 1.4; letter-spacing: 0.06em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--color-accent); }
  .strip-value { font-size: 0.875rem; line-height: 1.5; color: var(--color-ink-secondary); }

  .audit-list { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.75rem; }
  .audit-list li { font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--color-ink-secondary); padding-left: 1.25rem; position: relative; }
  .audit-list li::before { content: '→'; position: absolute; left: 0; color: var(--color-accent); }

  .deliverables-list, .process-list { display: flex; flex-direction: column; border: 1px solid var(--color-rule); border-radius: 4px; overflow: hidden; }
  .deliverable-item, .process-step { display: flex; gap: 1.25rem; align-items: flex-start; padding: 1.25rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-rule); background: var(--color-surface-secondary); }
  .deliverable-item:last-child, .process-step:last-child { border-bottom: none; }
  .item-num { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.75rem; letter-spacing: 0.1em; color: var(--color-accent); opacity: 0.75; flex-shrink: 0; padding-top: 0.15rem; min-width: 1.25rem; }
  .item-heading { font-size: 0.9375rem; font-weight: 500; color: var(--color-ink); margin-bottom: 0.35rem; }
  .item-body { font-size: 0.875rem; line-height: 1.7; color: var(--color-ink-tertiary); margin: 0; }

  .review-grid, .next-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 1px; background: var(--color-rule); border: 1px solid var(--color-rule); border-radius: 4px; overflow: hidden; }
  .review-item { background: var(--color-surface-secondary); padding: 1rem 1.25rem; font-size: 0.875rem; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--color-ink-secondary); }

  .next-card { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.55rem; background: var(--color-surface-secondary); padding: 1.25rem; text-decoration: none; transition: background 0.15s; }
  .next-card:hover { background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-surface-secondary) 90%, var(--color-accent)); }
  .next-card strong { font-family: var(--font-serif); font-size: 1.05rem; font-weight: 400; color: var(--color-ink); }
  .next-card > span:last-child { font-size: 0.875rem; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--color-ink-tertiary); }

  .engagement-panel { padding: 1.5rem; border: 1px solid var(--color-rule); border-left: 2px solid var(--color-accent); border-radius: 4px; background: var(--color-surface-secondary); }
  .engagement-panel .prose-section p { font-size: 0.9375rem; line-height: 1.75; }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .engagement-strip, .review-grid, .next-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .engagement-strip > div { flex-direction: row; justify-content: space-between; align-items: baseline; gap: 1rem; }
    .deliverable-item, .process-step { gap: 0.875rem; padding: 1rem; }
  }
</style>
